## 2. Milestone Implementation Breakdown

### M0 & M0.1 — Foundations & Web Server Seam (Completed)
- **Three-Crate Workspace:**
  - `crates/common`: Protocol types (`Operation`, `OperationResult`), versioned envelope (`PROTOCOL_VERSION = 1`), data transfer models.
  - `crates/panel`: Axum web framework, Askama compiled templates, SQLite control plane, job queue engine.
  - `crates/agent`: Node daemon with privileged command execution (`exec.rs`), resource isolation, and Docker/Nginx/MariaDB controllers.
- **Nginx Engine & Capability Probe:**
  - Host capability parser (`nginx -V`) testing HTTP/2 directives, brotli, and `ngx_cache_purge`.
  - Dialect-aware vhost generator and FastCGI cache configuration.

### M1 — Security Foundations (Completed)
- **CSRF Protection:** Per-session HMAC tokens validated on all state-mutating requests (`crates/panel/src/csrf.rs`).
- **Agent TLS Pinning:** Custom `rustls::client::danger::ServerCertVerifier` in `crates/panel/src/agent.rs` enforcing constant-time SHA-256 fingerprint verification of the agent leaf certificate. Insecure certificate bypass removed.
- **Login Throttling:** IP-based sliding window rate limiter (`crates/panel/src/auth.rs`) defending against brute-force attacks.
- **API Token Auth:** SHA-256 bearer tokens (`db/tokens.rs`, `require_api_auth` middleware) for CLI and API integrations.
- **RFC 6238 TOTP 2FA:** Hand-rolled TOTP implementation (`crates/panel/src/totp.rs`) with custom RFC 4648 Base32 encode/decode, 30-second time steps, settings enrollment UI, and a two-stage login challenge flow.

### M2 — WordPress Management (Completed)
- **Item Management:** Live inspection and management of WordPress plugins, themes, and users via WP-CLI.
- **Job Integration:** Typed actions (`plugin.action`, `theme.action`, `wpuser.reset_password`, `cron.run`) executed through background jobs.
- **Cache Purge Hooks:** Dedicated must-use plugin (`wp-content/mu-plugins/wp-panel-cache.php`) triggering Nginx FastCGI cache invalidation upon content updates.
- **Audit Trails:** Mutating WordPress actions logged to `audit_logs` table.

### M3 — Backups, Schedules & Restore (Completed)
- **Secret Encryption:** AES-256-GCM encryption (`crates/panel/src/secrets.rs`) for S3/MinIO destination credentials stored in SQLite.
- **Restic Protocol:** Ephemeral `ResticTarget` passed per-operation with zero secrets persisted on node agents.
- **Schedule Management UI:** Dedicated backup schedule editor per site (`templates/sites/backup_schedule.html`) with HTMX fragment loading supporting configurable scope (full, files only, database only) and intervals (6h, 12h, 24h, weekly).
- **Automated Scheduler:** Background scheduler loop (`crates/panel/src/scheduler.rs`) polling for due schedules and queueing backup jobs.

### M4 — Cloning & Staging (Completed)
- **Site Duplication:** Full site clone pipeline copying files via `rsync`, dumping/restoring databases, rewriting `wp-config.php`, running WP-CLI search-and-replace, and standing up PHP containers.
- **Staging Isolation:** Staging environments automatically configured with `blog_public = 0` and `WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE = staging`.
- **Staging Push:** Safe push mechanism requiring automated pre-push safety backups.

### M5 — Monitoring, Metrics & Alerts (Completed)
- **Host & Container Metrics:** System load, memory, disk, and per-container CPU/RAM/PHP-FPM worker metrics collected every heartbeat.
- **Sparkline Visualizations:** Pure inline SVG sparklines rendered without client-side JavaScript dependencies across server and site overview pages.
- **Site Metrics UI:** Real-time metrics fragment (`/partials/sites/{id}/metrics`) auto-polling every 30 seconds.
- **Alert System:** Background alert evaluator (`crates/panel/src/alerts.rs`) tracking disk usage (>85%), expiring SSL certificates (<14 days), offline sites, and stale backups with UI notification badges.

### M6 — Import Existing WordPress Sites (Completed)
- **Protocol Operations:** Added `InspectImportSource` and `ImportSite` operations to `wp-common`.
- **Agent Migration Engine:** 13-step pipeline (`crates/agent/src/ops/import.rs`) inspecting remote hosts via SSH, validating compatibility, copying filesystem data with `rsync`, exporting/importing databases, creating local `wp-config.php`, starting containers, performing URL search & replace, and validating core file checksums.
- **Panel Wizard:** 3-step wizard (`crates/panel/src/web/imports.rs`) guiding the operator from SSH connection probe to confirmation and job execution.

### M7 & §9.1 — Teams, Roles, Invitations & Multi-Tenant RBAC (Completed)
- **Database Schema:** `migrations/0005_teams.sql` adding `site_users` access table and `invitation_tokens` table.
- **Role Hierarchy:** Enforced hierarchy (`owner` > `admin` > `operator` > `viewer`) in `crates/panel/src/db/teams.rs`.
- **Multi-Tenant Query Scoping:** `db/sites.rs` implements `list_for_user()` and `get_for_user()`. Non-admin users (`operator`, `viewer`) are strictly constrained to sites explicitly assigned to them via `site_users`.
- **RBAC Mutation Gates:** `viewer` role is strictly read-only; all state-altering endpoints (site actions, plugins, themes, backups, limits, cache, console, import) enforce `require_operator_or_above` returning HTTP 403 Forbidden on violation.
- **Site Grant & Revoke Management:** Team administration UI in `/settings/users` allows owners and admins to view assigned sites and grant or revoke site access per operator/viewer.
- **Public Registration:** Self-service registration endpoint `/register?token=...` for onboarding invited team members.

### §9.1 — SMTP Email Delivery Integration (Completed)
- **Async SMTP Client:** Hand-rolled RFC 5321 async SMTP client (`crates/panel/src/email.rs`) with AUTH LOGIN and standard MIME headers over `tokio::net::TcpStream`.
- **Zero-Dependency Ergonomics:** Standard tokio and base64 used without adding unvetted third-party crates.
- **Config Parameters:** CLI and environment flags (`WP_PANEL_SMTP_HOST`, `WP_PANEL_SMTP_PORT`, `WP_PANEL_SMTP_USER`, `WP_PANEL_SMTP_PASSWORD`, `WP_PANEL_SMTP_FROM`).
- **Graceful Fallback:** When SMTP host is unconfigured, automatically logs the formatted email body to the tracing logger at `INFO` level.
- **UI Test & Invitation Delivery:** Automated invitation email dispatch upon inviting new users, and an on-demand "Send test email" endpoint (`POST /settings/smtp/test`) in the settings UI.

### §9.6 — Operations & Protocol Documentation (Completed)
- **Operations Runbook (`docs/OPERATIONS.md`):** Complete operations guide covering SQLite disaster recovery, key rotation, restic backup scopes, CLI emergency restore, rolling agent daemon upgrades, and triage matrix for HTTP 502/504 errors.
- **Protocol Catalog (`docs/PROTOCOL.md`):** Complete catalog of all 22 operations, wire envelope format, TLS pinning verification, request parameters, response schemas, step reports, and error payloads.

### X1 — CI Pipeline & Automated Testing (Completed)
- **CI Workflow:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` running `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`, and release artifact packaging.
- **Test Coverage (32 tests):**
  - 21 unit tests in `wp-agent` (capabilities, Nginx vhost generation, mu-plugin hooks, import dry-run).
  - 8 unit tests in `wp-panel` (crypto seal/open roundtrips, RFC 6238 TOTP test vectors, base32 roundtrip, SMTP unconfigured fallback, invitation payload formatting).
  - 4 HTTP integration tests in `crates/panel/tests/http.rs` testing health check, login redirects, login form rendering, and API authentication.

